{%- comment -%}
  Canonical serialization of a ledger entry payload (spec §6.1). SINGLE SOURCE OF
  TRUTH — both ledger/append (hashing a fresh entry) and ledger/verify_chain
  (re-hashing a stored entry read back from the DB) call this, so the hash is
  reproducible regardless of whether values arrive as native types or as strings
  from `property(name:)`.

  Determinism guarantees:
   - FIXED key order per version (this file defines it — string fields, then integer
     fields; version 1 puts canonical_version first).
   - Every key is ALWAYS emitted (absent → null), so shape never varies.
   - Explicit per-type coercion: integers via `| plus: 0` (→ JSON number),
     strings forced to string; blank → null. So "84" and 84 canonicalize
     identically, which is what makes DB round-tripping safe.

  The two hash fields (prev_entry_hash, entry_hash) are deliberately EXCLUDED —
  entry_hash is computed as digest(canonical || prev_entry_hash) by the caller.

  VERSIONED FORMAT. Each row stores the `canonical_version` it was hashed with, and
  this file picks the field list by that version, so a later format change (a new
  field, a different coercion) applies to new rows only and never breaks the chain
  over old ones. Never edit an existing version's field list: add a new version,
  set `current_canonical_version` in ledger/append to it, and keep the old branch.
    0 — rows written before versioning existed (blank canonical_version): the 22
        fields below, without canonical_version.
    1 — version 0's fields plus canonical_version itself (so the version cannot be
        altered without breaking the hash).
  An unknown version returns null; verify_chain reports it as a break.

  @param {object} entry - a hash (or GraphQL record) exposing the payload fields
  @return {string} canonical JSON of the payload with fixed key order
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign e = entry
  assign p = {}

  assign version = 0
  unless e.canonical_version == blank
    assign version = e.canonical_version | plus: 0
  endunless
  if version > 1 or version < 0
    return null
  endif
  if version >= 1
    assign p['canonical_version'] = version
  endif

  assign str_fields = 'occurred_at,method,tool_name,tool_version,client_id,agent_id,principal_id,delegation_mode,input_sha256,authz_policy,authz_decision,authz_reason,execution_outcome,subject_type,subject_id,idempotency_key,request_id,audit_json' | split: ','
  for f in str_fields
    assign v = e[f]
    if v == blank
      assign p[f] = null
    else
      assign p[f] = v | append: ''
    endif
  endfor

  assign int_fields = 'seq,input_bytes,error_code,duration_ms' | split: ','
  for f in int_fields
    assign v = e[f]
    if v == blank
      assign p[f] = null
    else
      assign p[f] = v | plus: 0
    endif
  endfor

  return p | json
%}
